["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The land squeezes deer onto a few lines. Sit beside one and the deer comes to you.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-trail-reeds.jpg\" alt=\"A deer trail pushed through grass. Packed soil and tracks in the middle.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A deer trail pushed through grass. Packed soil and tracks in the middle. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: MaryC2000, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_Trail.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>A trail is where animals walk again and again.</li><li>A funnel is where the land forces them onto one trail.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this session covers</summary><ul><li>A trail is where animals walk again and again. A funnel is where the land forces them onto one trail.</li><li>This session: trails, funnels, pinch points, saddles, benches, edges, bedding versus feeding, and how to turn all that into a stand or a glassing point.</li><li>Nearly all of this is hunter craft, not science. Treat it as a strong Tip and test it on your own ground.</li><li>Wind and thermals decide where you sit. Read <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">Wind and thermals</a> first.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Reading where a trail goes. Left: one trail splits into many faint lines, it is entering a feeding or bedding area. Right: many faint lines gather into one packed trail, it is heading for a crossing. Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Where is the trail going?</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"45\" width=\"185\" height=\"180\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"205\" y=\"45\" width=\"185\" height=\"180\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M100 215 V150\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M100 150 Q60 110 30 60\"/><path d=\"M100 150 Q85 100 75 55\"/><path d=\"M100 150 Q115 100 125 55\"/><path d=\"M100 150 Q140 110 175 60\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M225 60 Q260 120 297 150\"/><path d=\"M265 55 Q285 110 297 150\"/><path d=\"M330 55 Q310 110 297 150\"/><path d=\"M372 60 Q335 120 297 150\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M297 150 V215\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\"/>\n  <path d=\"M280 215 h34\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"8\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Splits apart</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">entering feed or beds</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gathers into one</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">heading to a crossing</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip: follow far enough to know both ends</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Packed, bare, 15 to 30 cm wide, with prints and pellets <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Find where it comes from and where it goes (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to read a trail</summary><ul><li>A game trail is a bare, packed line 15 to 30 cm wide through grass or duff, with hoof prints and pellets along it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Cattle trails are wider, deeper and churned, with cow pies. In Region 3 grassland many trails are shared (Tip).</li><li>Count the sign per 10 m of trail. Lots of fresh pellets and crisp prints: a highway. Old faded sign: a back road (Tip).</li><li>A trail that splits into many faint lines is entering a feeding or bedding area. A trail that gathers many lines into one is heading for a crossing (Tip).</li><li>Deer trails run on the easiest line: along a bench, round the head of a draw, through the low spot in a ridge <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Follow a trail far enough to answer two questions: where does it come from and where does it go (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 470\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"470\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bird's eye view: where the deer must walk</text>\n\n  <!-- bedding timber band, north slope -->\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"52\" width=\"380\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" fill-opacity=\"0.18\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M30 100 L40 72 L50 100 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M60 104 L70 76 L80 104 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 100 L100 72 L110 100 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M120 104 L130 76 L140 104 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M150 100 L160 72 L170 100 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M230 100 L240 72 L250 100 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M260 104 L270 76 L280 104 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M290 100 L300 72 L310 100 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M320 104 L330 76 L340 104 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M350 100 L360 72 L370 100 Z\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bedding: timber on the cool north slope</text>\n\n  <!-- two high points with the saddle between -->\n  <ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"88\" ry=\"42\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.45\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.45\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" fill-opacity=\"0.5\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"295\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"88\" ry=\"42\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.45\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"295\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.45\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"295\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" fill-opacity=\"0.5\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"62\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">High point</text>\n  <text x=\"338\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">High point</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Saddle</text>\n\n  <!-- bench: flat shelf below the ridge -->\n  <path d=\"M40 232 C120 222 280 222 360 232 L360 250 C280 240 120 240 40 250 Z\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"134\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Bench</text>\n\n  <!-- creek -->\n  <path d=\"M10 300 C60 290 90 320 130 305 C170 290 190 300 200 300 C230 300 250 312 290 300 C330 288 360 305 390 298\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <path d=\"M10 300 C60 290 90 320 130 305 C170 290 190 300 200 300 C230 300 250 312 290 300 C330 288 360 305 390 298\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"300\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Creek crossing = pinch point</text>\n\n  <!-- feeding field -->\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"350\" width=\"380\" height=\"72\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" fill-opacity=\"0.25\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M40 405 L44 393 L48 405\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 408 L94 396 L98 408\"/>\n    <path d=\"M140 404 L144 392 L148 404\"/>\n    <path d=\"M260 406 L264 394 L268 406\"/>\n    <path d=\"M310 403 L314 391 L318 403\"/>\n    <path d=\"M360 408 L364 396 L368 408\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"376\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feeding: grassland, cut block or hayfield</text>\n\n  <!-- deer movement arrows -->\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n    <path d=\"M200 112 L200 185\"/>\n    <path d=\"M70 112 C110 140 160 160 196 184\"/>\n    <path d=\"M330 112 C290 140 240 160 204 184\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 205 L200 232\"/>\n    <path d=\"M60 240 C110 238 160 260 196 292\"/>\n    <path d=\"M340 240 C290 238 240 260 204 292\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 250 L200 290\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 310 L200 360\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M200 192 L193 180 L207 180 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 240 L193 228 L207 228 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 296 L193 284 L207 284 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 368 L193 356 L207 356 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M198 186 L186 182 L192 172 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M202 186 L208 172 L214 182 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M198 294 L186 290 L190 280 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M202 294 L210 280 L214 290 Z\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\">deer lines</text>\n\n  <!-- the hunter -->\n  <path d=\"M285 262 L290 274 L303 275 L293 283 L296 296 L285 289 L274 296 L277 283 L267 275 L280 274 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"285\" y=\"257\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text>\n  <text x=\"309\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">100 to 150 m</text>\n  <text x=\"309\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">downwind</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\" fill=\"none\">\n    <line x1=\"222\" y1=\"268\" x2=\"256\" y2=\"268\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M264 268 L254 263 L254 273 Z\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"240\" y=\"287\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wind</text>\n\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"442\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bed above, feed below. Every line meets at the crossing.</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sit beside it, not on it.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Funnel: land that narrows the routes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Pinch point: the narrowest spot in it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 340\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four kinds of pinch point, seen from above, where deer must squeeze through. Creek crossing with low banks. A gap in a cliff band. An open gate or downed fence. The inside corner of a field. An orange dot marks where the deer lines meet.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 pinch points</text>\n  <g><rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"130\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 100 Q100 90 195 110\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"14\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <path d=\"M60 50 Q95 80 100 98 M140 50 Q110 80 100 98 M100 98 Q100 130 95 165\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"98\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"102\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Creek crossing</text></g>\n  <g><rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"130\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n    <path d=\"M205 95 H280 L290 110 H205 Z M310 110 L320 95 H390 V110 Z\" fill=\"#6f6252\"/>\n    <path d=\"M300 50 V160\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"102\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"297\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gap in a cliff band</text></g>\n  <g><rect x=\"10\" y=\"200\" width=\"185\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n    <path d=\"M10 255 H80 M120 255 H195\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <g fill=\"#6b4f35\"><rect x=\"76\" y=\"247\" width=\"6\" height=\"16\"/><rect x=\"118\" y=\"247\" width=\"6\" height=\"16\"/></g>\n    <path d=\"M60 210 Q100 240 100 255 M140 210 Q100 240 100 255 M100 255 V305\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"255\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"102\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gate or downed fence</text></g>\n  <g><rect x=\"205\" y=\"200\" width=\"185\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/>\n    <path d=\"M205 200 H390 V230 H245 V310 H205 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <path d=\"M300 230 Q270 250 255 240 M330 290 Q270 270 255 240\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"252\" cy=\"238\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">field</text>\n    <text x=\"297\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Inside field corner</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: saddles, benches, edges and crossings</summary><ul><li>A <strong>funnel</strong> is any feature that narrows the possible routes: a strip of timber between two openings, a creek bottom, a bench, a cut block edge <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>A <strong>pinch point</strong> is the narrowest spot in a funnel: a creek crossing, a gap in a cliff band, an open gate or a downed fence, the inside corner of a field <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Saddles: the low dip between two high points on a ridge. Deer cross ridges here, hidden from the skyline and using the least effort <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Benches: flat shelves on a hillside. Deer walk them and bed on them <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Edges: where two cover types meet, like timber against grassland or an old burn against green forest. Deer feed on the edge and bed just inside <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Water crossings: deer cross creeks where banks are low and gravel is firm. One crossing may serve a whole slope (Tip).</li><li>In the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Rut\">Rut</button>, bucks cruise funnels between doe groups. A saddle between two bedding ridges is a November classic <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, bird's eye view. A deer starts bedded in timber at the top. At dusk it walks down the trail to the open feeding field and feeds through the night. At dawn it walks back up the same trail to bed. Final label: hunt the line between bed and feed, near the feed at dusk, near the bed at dawn.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,100 42,62 54,100\"/><polygon points=\"80,95 92,57 104,95\"/><polygon points=\"300,100 312,62 324,100\"/><polygon points=\"350,95 362,57 374,95\"/><polygon points=\"250,90 262,52 274,90\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Feed: open field</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"44\" width=\"155\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" opacity=\".85\"/>\n  <text x=\"198\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bed: timber</text>\n  <path id=\"sg-bed-feed-down\" d=\"M200 95 C 240 130, 160 170, 210 250\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n  <path id=\"sg-bed-feed-loop\" d=\"M200 95 C 240 130, 160 170, 210 250 C 160 170, 240 130, 200 95\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"none\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"38\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Day: bedded, chewing cud\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"1.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f2a56b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Dusk: down to feed\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1.5s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#cfd8e6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Night: feeding in the open\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"5.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Dawn: back up to bed\n      <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <ellipse rx=\"13\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"-5\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n    <animateMotion dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\" keyPoints=\"0;0;0.5;0.5;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1875;0.5;0.6875;1\"><mpath href=\"#sg-bed-feed-loop\"/></animateMotion>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"215\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"254\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">You at dusk</text>\n    <circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"130\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"259\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">You at dawn</text>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"258\" width=\"320\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt the line between</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Watch the daily loop. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Feed in the open at dusk and dawn, bed hidden by day <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Never hunt inside the beds. Hunt the line <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: bed and feed in detail</summary><ul><li>Feeding areas are open: grassland, cut blocks, hayfields, burns with new shrubs, a south slope with saskatoon and bitterbrush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Bedding areas are hidden: timber on a north slope, a bench with a view below, the top third of a ridge, thick regrowth <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Deer feed in the open at dusk and dawn, then move to bed as the light grows <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Morning trails run uphill, evening trails run downhill (Tip).</li><li>Mule deer near Heffley Creek: grassland and open Douglas fir benches to feed, timber and broken rock above to bed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>White tails: hayfields and cottonwood bottoms to feed, thick brush and willows to bed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Never hunt inside the bedding area. Hunt the line between bed and feed: closer to the bed in the morning, closer to the feed in the evening (hunter lore) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grass-fir-edge.jpg\" alt=\"The edge: feed in the grass, bed in the trees.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The edge: feed in the grass, bed in the trees. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andres Alvarado, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_colorful_of_Lac_Du_Bois_Grasslands.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-lac-du-bois-grassland.jpg\" alt=\"Open bunchgrass: feeding ground.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Open bunchgrass: feeding ground. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: tuchodi, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lac_du_Bois_Grasslands_Protected_Area_(4043429977).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-douglas-fir-stand.jpg\" alt=\"Douglas fir timber: bedding cover.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Douglas fir timber: bedding cover. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Lavin from Bozeman, Montana, USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pseudotsuga_menziesii_subsp._glauca_(Interior_Douglas-fir),_Wild_Horse_Island,_Montana_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Pick a stand in 4 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 1: find the line. A trail or funnel runs between a known bed in the timber and a known feeding field.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,100 42,62 54,100\"/><polygon points=\"90,95 102,57 114,95\"/><polygon points=\"300,100 312,62 324,100\"/><polygon points=\"355,95 367,57 379,95\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"215\" width=\"400\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Bed, uphill</text>\n<path d=\"M180 105 C 220 140, 150 180, 200 225\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Find the line</text>\n<rect x=\"140\" y=\"95\" width=\"100\" height=\"140\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">The line</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">bed to feed</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Find the line between bed and feed.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 2: check the wind and the thermal for the hour you will sit. Morning air rises, so sit above or beside the line. Evening air sinks, so sit below or beside it.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,100 42,62 54,100\"/><polygon points=\"90,95 102,57 114,95\"/><polygon points=\"300,100 312,62 324,100\"/><polygon points=\"355,95 367,57 379,95\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"215\" width=\"400\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Bed, uphill</text>\n<path d=\"M180 105 C 220 140, 150 180, 200 225\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Check wind for that hour</text>\n<g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M60 200 V130\"/><path d=\"M50 142 l10 -14 l10 14\"/><path d=\"M340 130 V200\"/><path d=\"M330 188 l10 14 l10 -14\"/></g><text x=\"60\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" dx=\"14\">sit above</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening</text><text x=\"326\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">sit below</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Check the wind for the hour you sit.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 3: pick a spot 100 to 200 m off the line with a long view, a solid rest for the rifle, and earth behind every shooting lane, not sky.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,100 42,62 54,100\"/><polygon points=\"90,95 102,57 114,95\"/><polygon points=\"300,100 312,62 324,100\"/><polygon points=\"355,95 367,57 379,95\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"215\" width=\"400\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Bed, uphill</text>\n<path d=\"M180 105 C 220 140, 150 180, 200 225\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Sit 100 to 200 m off it</text>\n<circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M309 150 H215\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><text x=\"265\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 to 200 m</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">rest, view,</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">earth backstop</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Sit 100 to 200 m off it, solid rest.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 4: plan a quiet approach that never crosses the trail, the feed or the bed. Come in from behind. Pick a B spot for the opposite wind.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,100 42,62 54,100\"/><polygon points=\"90,95 102,57 114,95\"/><polygon points=\"300,100 312,62 324,100\"/><polygon points=\"355,95 367,57 379,95\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"215\" width=\"400\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#e9dfa8\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Feed</text>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Bed, uphill</text>\n<path d=\"M180 105 C 220 140, 150 180, 200 225\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. Come in the back way</text>\n<path d=\"M400 175 C 375 172, 355 160, 332 152\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"390\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">back way in</text><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"160\" r=\"11\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B spot</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Come in the back way. Keep a B spot.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Check the earth <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Backstop\">Backstop</button> behind every lane (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all 7 steps and my lean</summary><ol><li>Find the line: a trail or funnel between a known bed and a known feed (Tip).</li><li>Check the wind and the thermal for the hour you will sit. Morning: sit above or beside the line. Evening: sit below or beside it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Pick a spot 100 to 200 m off the line with a long view and a solid rest for the rifle. Past 200 m you are a watcher, not a shooter (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/glassing\">Glassing</a>.</li><li>Check the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Backstop\">Backstop</button> behind every lane you might shoot. Earth, not sky (Tip).</li><li>Plan a quiet approach that does not cross the trail, the feed or the bed. Come in the back way (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/still-hunting\">Moving quietly</a>.</li><li>Pick a B spot for the opposite wind. Never force A (Tip).</li><li>Mark it on your map and note where the sun will rise. A low sun in your face kills glassing (Tip).</li></ol><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>For your first October trips, pick a glassing point above a grassland edge with timber behind you. Sit from 45 minutes before legal light. Learn the lines first, then move closer.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 540\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"ct-arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"540\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Side view of the hill</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" fill=\"none\">\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"80\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"110\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"140\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"170\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"200\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"85\">1400 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"115\">1300 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"145\">1200 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"175\">1100 m</text>\n    <text x=\"4\" y=\"205\">1000 m</text>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M 60,218 C 75,212 90,195 105,170 C 120,140 140,100 160,82 C 170,73 182,72 190,80 C 200,92 212,112 222,124 C 230,132 240,132 248,124 C 258,112 268,96 278,86 C 284,80 292,80 298,88 C 310,110 316,150 322,166 L 350,168 C 362,170 376,196 390,218 L 395,218 L 395,232 L 60,232 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"178\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"288\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"236\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Saddle</text>\n  <text x=\"354\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bench</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Steep</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">lines close</text>\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"248\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"248\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same hill from above: contours</text>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <path d=\"M 15,395 C 15,330 80,300 140,300 C 185,300 196,335 220,348 C 246,360 256,328 290,325 C 360,322 398,372 394,420 C 388,458 350,478 300,476 C 270,476 255,480 245,478 C 232,476 226,440 218,432 C 210,440 200,478 182,480 C 152,484 120,482 100,474 C 60,464 32,450 14,425 C 6,412 8,402 15,395 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 35,395 C 35,345 90,318 140,318 C 180,318 192,348 216,360 C 240,372 250,345 286,342 C 340,340 390,372 386,418 C 380,448 350,462 302,460 C 282,459 264,462 252,460 C 240,458 230,432 218,422 C 206,432 196,458 182,460 C 155,463 128,462 108,456 C 76,448 50,440 36,418 C 29,408 30,400 35,395 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 62,392 C 62,350 108,332 140,334 C 172,336 186,360 212,372 C 234,382 246,362 282,360 C 326,358 350,382 346,412 C 342,438 322,448 290,446 C 262,444 246,428 214,422 C 196,422 182,446 142,448 C 100,450 62,430 62,392 Z\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"388\" rx=\"42\" ry=\"26\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"288\" cy=\"400\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"22\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"388\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"12\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"288\" cy=\"400\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"11\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 112,357 Q 140,347 168,357\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 110,352 Q 140,341 170,352\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 108,347 Q 140,335 172,347\"/>\n  </g>\n  <line x1=\"140\" y1=\"388\" x2=\"288\" y2=\"400\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"393\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"288\" y=\"405\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak</text>\n  <text x=\"214\" y=\"407\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ridge</text>\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#ct-arrow)\">\n    <line x1=\"214\" y1=\"302\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"382\"/>\n    <line x1=\"84\" y1=\"302\" x2=\"118\" y2=\"342\"/>\n    <line x1=\"236\" y1=\"498\" x2=\"221\" y2=\"440\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"512\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"432\"/>\n    <line x1=\"366\" y1=\"482\" x2=\"366\" y2=\"420\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"214\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Saddle</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cliff</text>\n  <text x=\"396\" y=\"496\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Bench: wide gap</text>\n  <text x=\"236\" y=\"514\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Draw: V points uphill</text>\n  <text x=\"14\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Spur: V points downhill</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Lines close: steep. Dip in a ridge: saddle. Wide gap: bench <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Mark saddles, benches and crossings before you walk (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: map scouting, cameras and drones</summary><ul><li>Use a topographic map or iMapBC, the province's online map, to find saddles, benches and creek crossings before you walk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Contour lines close together: steep. A ridge line with a dip in it: a saddle. A wide gap between lines on a hillside: a bench <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Satellite view shows cut blocks, burns, hayfields and timber edges. Mark each, then mark the narrowest strip of cover between them (Tip).</li><li>Walk the ground in daylight, at midday when deer are bedded, and from downwind of the bedding (Tip).</li><li>Trail cameras work on funnels. A wireless camera is illegal for hunting from 1 August to 10 December in every region except Region 1, where wireless cameras for hunting are banned all year (page 20) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Use a memory card camera (85%, interpretation).</li><li>Drones are illegal on a hunting expedition <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Consent for cultivated land and grazed leases <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td><td>page 12, item 53</td></tr><tr><td>No wireless camera for hunting, 1 August to 10 December <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td><td>page 11, item 30</td></tr><tr><td>No drone on a hunting trip <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td><td>page 11, item 36</td></tr><tr><td>No motor vehicles above 1,700 m off roads, Region 3 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td><td>page 33</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the rules in full</summary><ul><li>You may not hunt on cultivated land, or on Crown land under a grazing lease while livestock are on it, without the consent of the owner, lessee or occupant <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Synopsis page 12, item 53.</li><li>It is unlawful to use a wireless camera for the purposes of hunting from 1 August to 10 December in every region except Region 1, where wireless cameras for hunting are banned all year (99%, page 20). Synopsis page 11, item 30 (2 October 2026 edition).</li><li>It is unlawful to operate or possess a drone on a hunting or trapping expedition <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Synopsis page 11, item 36 (2 October 2026 edition).</li><li>Region 3: all motor vehicles except snowmobiles are prohibited above 1,700 m elevation except on existing roads and trails <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Region 3 synopsis page 33. Many good saddles are above that line; walk in.</li><li>Ask yourself where the deer will fall. A trail on the far side of a creek can mean a wet pack out (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Find the bed, find the feed, then sit on the line between them with the wind in your face. Everything else is detail.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Sitting right on the trail. Your scent and your shape are on the line the deer must use.</li><li>Walking through the feeding field at dusk to reach the stand. Every deer saw you.</li><li>Picking a stand for the view and ignoring the wind.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>On a scouting day: walk one trail from an open feeding area uphill until it hits timber. Mark where it splits, every pinch point and every crossing. Pick one glassing point for a morning west wind and one for an evening east wind.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grass-fir-edge.jpg\" alt=\"Bed in the trees, feed in the grass, you on the line.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bed in the trees, feed in the grass, you on the line. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andres Alvarado, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_colorful_of_Lac_Du_Bois_Grasslands.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Find the bed, find the feed, then sit on the line between them with the wind in your face. Everything else is detail.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Sitting right on the trail. Your scent and your shape are on the line the deer must use.</li><li>Walking through the feeding field at dusk to reach the stand. Every deer saw you.</li><li>Picking a stand for the view and ignoring the wind.</li></ul></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Reading where a trail goes. Left: one trail splits into many faint lines, it is entering a feeding or bedding area. Right: many faint lines gather into one packed trail, it is heading for a crossing. Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Where is the trail going?</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"45\" width=\"185\" height=\"180\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"205\" y=\"45\" width=\"185\" height=\"180\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M100 215 V150\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M100 150 Q60 110 30 60\"/><path d=\"M100 150 Q85 100 75 55\"/><path d=\"M100 150 Q115 100 125 55\"/><path d=\"M100 150 Q140 110 175 60\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M225 60 Q260 120 297 150\"/><path d=\"M265 55 Q285 110 297 150\"/><path d=\"M330 55 Q310 110 297 150\"/><path d=\"M372 60 Q335 120 297 150\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M297 150 V215\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\"/>\n  <path d=\"M280 215 h34\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"8\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Splits apart</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">entering feed or beds</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gathers into one</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">heading to a crossing</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip: follow far enough to know both ends</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Scouting day: walk one trail from feed uphill to timber. Mark every split, pinch point and crossing.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full drill</summary><ul><li>On a scouting day: walk one trail from an open feeding area uphill until it hits timber. Mark where it splits, every pinch point and every crossing.</li><li>Pick one glassing point for a morning west wind and one for an evening east wind.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full synopsis</a>, read directly from the downloaded synopsis text: page 11 items 30 and 36, page 12 item 53; Region 3 page 33 (motor vehicles above 1,700 m). Checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Search previews (direct reading blocked in this environment), checked 2026-10-01, hunter craft capped at 60% to 65%:<ul><li><a href=\"https://bowhuntersunited.com/2020/10/01/how-terrain-funnels-deer-movements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bowhunters United, how terrain funnels deer movements</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.huntstand.com/fieldnotes/8-ways-to-find-killer-deer-hunting-funnels/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HuntStand, 8 ways to find killer deer hunting funnels</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.themeateater.com/wired-to-hunt/whitetail-hunting/how-to-use-terrain-and-topography-to-hunt-new-properties\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MeatEater, how to use terrain and topography</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.letsgohunting.org/resources/articles/big-game/how-to-read-topographic-maps-for-deer-hunting/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Let's Go Hunting, topographic maps for deer</a></li></ul></li></ul>","<ul><li>Staudenmaier and others 2021, <a href=\"https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ecs2.3813\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mule deer and white tail habitat</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>: mule deer on steep open ground, white tails in valley bottoms and fields.</li></ul><ul><li>Stewart and others 2002, <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/jmammal/article/84/3/1076/905056\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">deer activity timing</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>: dawn and dusk peaks.</li></ul><ul><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-01-deer.md</code> (bedding, local reading).</li></ul>"]